# noXa English ST13 authoring model card

Selected voice: ST13, "Eisbrecher", a synthetic adult voice used for both
English and German. Definition: tools/voices/ST13.json.

Model: Supertonic 3 (Supertone Inc.), 31 languages, flow-matching TTS.
Weights: OpenRAIL-M, https://huggingface.co/Supertone/supertonic-3
Conversion: sherpa-onnx INT8 release asset
sherpa-onnx-supertonic-3-tts-int8-2026-05-11.tar.bz2
SHA-256 82fa96f91c4ef8abaae3a14a3f4153facf88bed821d1f7331cec2700f432c427
Runtime: sherpa-onnx v1.13.8 (Apache-2.0), CPU, 2 threads, 8 flow steps.

Voice: weighted blend of the preset style vectors (M5 × 1.25, M1 × −0.25),
speed 0.97, language code en. No reference recording, no actor recording
and no imitation of an identifiable character.

Pronunciation: provenance.json pronunciation_aliases.en is applied as whole-word
respelling before synthesis; metrics.json renderText records the exact input.

Output: 44.1 kHz model output, FFT-resampled to 24 kHz mono PCM16 and mastered
by tools/generate-speech.py (trim, DC removal, 6 ms fades, -31 dBFS RMS,
0.115 peak ceiling).

Review: Whisper small transcribes every clip; a clip is accepted only when its
transcript contains every intended word. st13-content-review.json records the
transcript per shipped hash. This is not a human listening assessment.
